  "body": "|`docker run -it --rm \\\r\n    --mount type=volume,src=synapse-data,dst=/data \\\r\n    -e SYNAPSE_SERVER_NAME=my.matrix.host \\\r\n    -e SYNAPSE_REPORT_STATS=yes \\\r\n    matrixdotorg/synapse:latest generate`\r\n\r\nI use this command from the docker hub page. But I only get this homeserver.yaml file:\r\n\r\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/87895556/180995806-14b4331f-12eb-4ce5-bfbf-4c1478c8ff52.png)\r\n\r\nI wanna use postgres as database and I know that some people get bigger config files with much more default settings like this:\r\n[https://comatrix.eu/setup/matrix_synapse_homeserver/](url)\r\n\r\nDoes someone know why some people get different yaml files or are these big yaml files just old versions?",
